@startuml
title UC-02 — Manage Availability
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBEA
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C8BE8A
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ActorBorderColor #334155
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}
actor "Staff" as staffActor
boundary "planning:StaffPlanningBoundary" as planningUI #EAF3FC
control "planning:StaffPlanningController" as planning #ECF5ED
entity "availability:StaffAvailability" as availability #FFF9E8
entity "audit:AuditEntry" as audit #FFF9E8
database "Database" as db #F1F5F9
boundary "notifications:NotificationBoundary" as notifications #EAF3FC
actor "Manager" as manager

note over planningUI, planning
  Precondition: staff member is logged in.
  Trigger: enter or change their own availability.
  staffId comes from the authenticated user.
end note

' Main 1–2: own saved availability and the five-week shift choices.
staffActor -> planningUI : submit("open availability", ownUserContext)
planningUI -> planning : openAvailability(staffId)
planning -> db : Retrieve this staff member's saved availability\nand dated day/night shifts in the five-week planning period
db --> planning : previousAvailability, planningShifts
planning -> planningUI : display("availability",\npreviousAvailability and planningShifts)
planningUI --> staffActor : Show saved availability and selectable shifts
note over planningUI, availability
  Each selectable day or night shift lasts 12 hours.
  The form is restricted to the five-week planning period.
end note

' Main 3–4: local selection followed by submission.
staffActor -> planningUI : Indicate available shifts in the form
staffActor -> planningUI : submit("save availability", submission)
planningUI -> planning : saveAvailability(staffId, submission)
note right of planning
  Capture submittedAt on receipt.
  Wednesday cut-offs are evaluated separately
  for each submitted roster week.
  Exact cut-off time is a supplied policy value.
end note

' Main 5 and alternative 5a1: mixed on-time/late weeks are possible.
loop for each submitted roster week
  alt submittedAt is after this week's Wednesday cut-off
    planning -> availability : prepareWeek(rosterWeek, weekAvailability, true)
    availability --> planning : preparedWeek (affected availability has lateFlag = true)
  else submittedAt is on or before this week's Wednesday cut-off
    planning -> availability : prepareWeek(rosterWeek, weekAvailability, false)
    availability --> planning : preparedWeek (lateFlag = false)
  end
end
note right of planning
  preparedAvailability contains every submitted week.
  lateWeeks contains only the weeks flagged late.
end note

' Main 6; I01 reconciles the omitted save in alternative 5a.
planning -> db : Save submitted availability and per-week late flags\nfor this staff member within the five-week planning period
db --> planning : savedAvailability
note over planning, db
  Both on-time and late submissions are saved.
  Existing published assignments remain unchanged.
end note

' Main 7 and alternative 5a2: save precedes audit and visibility.
planning -> audit : recordChange("availability changed", staffId, submittedAt,\npreviousAvailability, savedAvailability, null)
audit --> planning : auditData
planning -> db : Append auditData to the audit log
db --> planning : auditRecorded
note over planning, db
  The saved availability, including affected late flags,
  is now available to managers for roster planning.
end note

' Alternative 5a3: only the late weeks require a manager notification.
opt one or more submitted roster weeks are late
  planning -> notifications : notify(managerId, "late availability",\nstaffId and affected lateWeeks and savedAvailability)
  notifications -> manager : Present late submissions or changes for consideration
end

' Main 8 and alternative 5a4: common successful completion.
planning -> planningUI : display("availability saved", savedAvailability)
planningUI --> staffActor : Confirm that availability has been saved
note over staffActor, manager
  Postconditions: own submitted availability and late flags are stored;
  managers can see the saved availability; an audit record exists.
  Any late submission or change has been notified to the manager.
  Published assignments are unchanged. Any subsequent amendment
  requires an authorised manager through UC-06 Amend Published Roster.
end note

legend bottom
  UML 2.5. Boundaries, controllers and operations are proposed detailed design (I08).
  Database requests describe persistence; no SQL schema is assumed.
  I01: late-branch persistence is explicit to satisfy the source postconditions.
endlegend
@enduml
